Farm Research Program for 8 years, developing soil amendment protocols adopted by over 200 organic farms nationwide. Author of Living Soil: A Practical Guide to Regenerative Gardening (Rodale Books). Active reviewer for the Soil Science Society of America Journal.\"}]]}]\n6:[\"$\",\"$L2\",\"922\",{\"href\":\"/authors/lisa-thompson\",\"className\":\"group flex flex-col items-center text-center p-6 bg-white border border-[var(--color-border)] rounded-xl hover:shadow-md hover:border-[var(--color-primary)] transition-all\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative w-20 h-20 rounded-full overflow-hidden mb-4 bg-[var(--color-muted)]\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"src\":\"https://s.alicdn.com/@sc02/kf/Add7ab32a241b446b84e0fca7d7d67899R.jpg\",\"alt\":\"Lisa Thompson\",\"fill\":true,\"sizes\":\"80px\",\"className\":\"object-cover\"}]}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"font-bold text-base group-hover:text-[var(--color-primary)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Lisa Thompson\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-[var(--color-muted-fg)] mt-2 line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"Award-winning landscape designer with 17 years of residential design experience and over 800 completed projects. Holds a B.L.A. in Landscape Architecture from the University of Florida and is a registered Landscape Architect (RLA) in 4 states. Her designs have been featured in Better Homes and Gardens, Southern Living, and the APLD International Design Awards. Pioneered the SmartScape Method for creating beautiful low-maintenance gardens that reduce water usage by up to 60% while increasing property value.\"}]]}]\n7:[\"$\",\"$L2\",\"923\",{\"href\":\"/authors/robert-hayes\",\"className\":\"group flex flex-col items-center text-center p-6 bg-white border border-[var(--color-border)] rounded-xl hover:shadow-md hover:border-[var(--color-primary)] transition-all\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative w-20 h-20 rounded-full overflow-hidden mb-4 bg-[v